body:
Given the following code ([playground](https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/91752)):

```rust
#![feature(rustc_attrs)]
#![feature(min_specialization)]
#![feature(const_trait_impl)]

#[rustc_specialization_trait]
trait Specialize {}

trait Foo {}

impl<T> const Foo for T {}

impl<T> const Foo for T
where
    T: ~const Specialize
{}
```

The following error is produced:

```
error: cannot specialize on `Binder(~const TraitPredicate(<T as Specialize>, polarity:Positive), [])`
  --> src/main.rs:12:1
   |
12 | / impl<T> const Foo for T
13 | | where
14 | |     T: ~const Specialize
15 | | {}
   | |__^
```

What I expect is that the compilation succeeds, as it does without the const trait impl and corresponding `~const` trait bound ([playground](https://play.rust-lang.org/?version=nightly&mode=debug&edition=2021&gist=d967a74cc12ef329c888b40d07c8e2c3)):

```rust
#![feature(rustc_attrs)]
#![feature(min_specialization)]

#[rustc_specialization_trait]
trait Specialize {}

trait Foo {}

impl<T> Foo for T {}

impl<T> Foo for T
where
    T: Specialize
{}
```

@rustbot label +F-const_trait_impl +F-specialization +A-specialization +A-traits

